#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:4
msgid "The effect of dependencies on ``package_id``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:6
msgid ""
"When a given package depends on a another package and uses it, the effect of "
"dependencies can be different based on the package types:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:8
msgid "For libraries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:10
msgid ""
"**Non-embed mode**: When an application or a shared library depends on "
"another shared library, or when a static library depends on another static "
"library, the \"consumer\" library does not do a copy of the binary artifacts "
"of the \"dependency\" at all. We call it non-embed mode, the dependency "
"binaries are not being linked or embedded in the consumer. This assumes that "
"there are not inlined functionalities in the dependency headers, and the "
"headers are pure interface and not implementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:11
msgid ""
"**Embed mode**: When an application or a shared library depends on a header-"
"only or a static-library, the dependencies binaries are copied or partially "
"copied (depending on the linker) in the consumer binary. Also when a static "
"library depends on a header-only library, it is considered that there will "
"be embedding in the consumer binary of such headers, as they will also "
"contain the implementation, it is impossible that they are a pure interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:13
msgid "For header-only libraries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:15
msgid ""
"Header only libraries are always independent of their dependencies, because "
"they do not link them. No change in the dependencies versions changes the "
"final package of the header-only library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:17
msgid "For applications (``tool_requires``):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:19
msgid ""
"**Build mode**: When some package uses a ``tool_requires`` of another "
"package, the binary artifacts in the dependency are never copied or embedded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:21
msgid ""
"When the package types are not known (the recipes do not define the "
"``shared`` option, or they do not define ``package_type`` attribute):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:23
msgid ""
"**Unknown mode**: This mode is generally not recommended, as it is the "
"result of not having enough information about the package types, and it "
"results in a excesively optimistic ``package_id`` computation with a "
"``semver`` approach for binary rebuilds, which is generally insufficient for "
"C and C++ libraries. The recommendation is to clear specify the ``shared`` "
"option or to explicitly define ``package_type``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:27
#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:205
msgid "Non-embed mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:29
msgid ""
"When we list the binaries of a package like ``openssl`` with dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:31
msgid ""
"$ conan list openssl/3.1.2:* -r=conancenter\n"
"conancenter\n"
"  openssl\n"
"    openssl/3.1.2\n"
"      revisions\n"
"        8879e931d726a8aad7f372e28470faa1 (2023-09-13 18:52:54 UTC)\n"
"          packages\n"
"            0348efdcd0e319fb58ea747bb94dbd88850d6dd1  # package_id\n"
"              info\n"
"                options\n"
"                  shared: True\n"
"                ...\n"
"                requires\n"
"                  zlib/1.3.Z"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:49
msgid ""
"This binary was a ``shared`` library, linking with ``zlib`` as a shared "
"library. This means it was using \"non-embed\" mode. The default of non-"
"embed mode is ``minor_mode``, which means:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:52
msgid ""
"All ``zlib`` patch versions will be mapped to the same ``zlib/1.3.Z``. This "
"means that if our ``openssl/3.1.2`` package binary "
"``0348efdcd0e319fb58ea747bb94dbd88850d6dd1`` binary is considered binary "
"compatible with all ``zlib/1.3.Z`` versions (for any ``Z``), and will not "
"require to rebuild the ``openssl`` binary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:53
msgid ""
"New ``zlib`` minor versions, like ``zlib/1.4.0`` will result in a \"minor-"
"mode\" identifier like ``zlib/1.4.Z``, and then, it will require a new "
"``openssl/3.1.2`` package binary, with a new ``package_id``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:58
msgid ""
"There was a bug in Conan versions previous to Conan 2.28 in this **non-embed "
"mode**, in which transitive dependencies could affect the ``package_id`` of "
"consumers, even if they were not direct dependencies, they were not being "
"embedded, and they were not propagating headers to it. This was causing sub-"
"optimal behavior, that could require some unnecessary builds from source for "
"new ``package_ids``. To avoid breaking existing users, this bug fix was "
"introduced as opt-in via policies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:63
msgid ""
"If a recipe defines ``required_conan_version = \">=2.28\"`` or higher, it "
"will automatically enable the new fixed ``package_id`` computation. Recipes "
"that don't update their required Conan version will still use the older "
"``package_id``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:65
msgid ""
"If the global configuration in ``global.conf`` defines the ``core:"
"policies=[\"required_conan_version>=2.28\"]`` it will have the same "
"behavior, enabling this bugfix for all packages. See the :ref:`documentation "
"for policies<reference_policies>` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:67
msgid ""
"The recommendation is to activate the new behavior via policies. It will "
"save resources like build time, and it will also be more future-proof, "
"future Conan versions might enable this behavior unconditionally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:73
#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:196
msgid "Embed mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:75
msgid ""
"The following commands illustrate the concept of embed-mode. We create a "
"``dep/0.1`` package with a static library, and then we create a ``app/0.1`` "
"package with an executable that links with static library inside "
"``dep/0.1``. We can use the ``conan new`` command for quickly creating these "
"two packages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:78
msgid ""
"$ mkdir dep && cd dep\n"
"$ conan new cmake_lib -d name=dep -d version=0.1\n"
"$ conan create . -tf=\"\"\n"
"$ cd .. && mkdir app && cd app\n"
"$ conan new cmake_exe -d name=app -d version=0.1 -d requires=dep/0.1\n"
"$ conan create .\n"
"dep/0.1: Hello World Release!\n"
"...\n"
"app/0.1: Hello World Release!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:90
msgid ""
"If we now list the ``app/0.1`` binaries, we will see the binary just created:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:93
msgid ""
"  $ conan list app/0.1:*\n"
"  Local Cache\n"
"    app/0.1\n"
"      revisions\n"
"        632e236936211ac2293ec33339ce582b (2023-09-25 22:34:17 UTC)\n"
"          packages\n"
"            3ca530d20914cf632eb00efbccc564da48190314\n"
"              info\n"
"                settings\n"
"                  ...\n"
"                requires\n"
"                  dep/0.1#d125304fb1fb088d5b92d4f8135f4dff:9bdee485ef71c14ac5f8a657202632bdb8b4482b"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:109
msgid ""
"It is now visible that the ``app/0.1`` package-id depends on the full "
"identifier of the ``dep/0.1`` dependency, that includes both its recipe "
"revision and ``package_id``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:111
msgid ""
"If we do a change now to the ``dep`` code, and re-create the ``dep/0.1`` "
"package , even if we don't bump the version, it will create a new recipe "
"revision:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:114
msgid ""
"$ cd ../dep\n"
"# Change the \"src/dep.cpp\" code to print a new message, like \"Hello "
"Moon\"\n"
"$ conan create . -tf=\"\"\n"
"# New recipe revision dep/0.1#1c90e8b8306c359b103da31faeee824c"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:121
msgid ""
"So if we try now to install ``app/0.1`` binary, it will fail with a "
"\"missing binary\" error:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:124
msgid ""
"  $ conan install --requires=app/0.1\n"
"  ERROR: Missing binary: app/0.1:ef2b5ed33d26b35b9147c90b27b217e2c7bde2d0\n"
"\n"
"  app/0.1: WARN: Can't find a 'app/0.1' package binary "
"'ef2b5ed33d26b35b9147c90b27b217e2c7bde2d0' for the configuration:\n"
"  [settings]\n"
"  ...\n"
"  [requires]\n"
"  dep/0.1#1c90e8b8306c359b103da31faeee824c:9bdee485ef71c14ac5f8a657202632bdb8b4482b\n"
"\n"
"  ERROR: Missing prebuilt package for 'app/0.1'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:139
msgid ""
"As the ``app`` executable links with the ``dep`` static library, it needs to "
"be rebuilt to include the latest changes, even if ``dep/0.1`` didn't bump "
"its version, ``app/0.1`` depends on \"embed-mode\" on ``dep/0.1``, so it wil "
"use down to the ``package_id`` of such dependency identifier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:141
msgid "Let's build the new ``app/0.1`` binary:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:143
msgid ""
"  $ cd ../app\n"
"  $ conan create .\n"
"  dep/0.1: Hello Moon Release!  # Message changed to Moon\n"
"  ...\n"
"  app/0.1: Hello World Release!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:152
msgid "Now we will have two ``app/0.1`` different binaries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:154
msgid ""
"  $ conan list \"app/0.1:*\"\n"
"  Local Cache\n"
"    app\n"
"      app/0.1\n"
"        revisions\n"
"          632e236936211ac2293ec33339ce582b (2023-09-25 22:49:32 UTC)\n"
"            packages\n"
"              3ca530d20914cf632eb00efbccc564da48190314\n"
"                info\n"
"                  settings\n"
"                    ...\n"
"                  requires\n"
"                    dep/0.1#d125304fb1fb088d5b92d4f8135f4dff:9bdee485ef71c14ac5f8a657202632bdb8b4482b\n"
"              ef2b5ed33d26b35b9147c90b27b217e2c7bde2d0\n"
"                info\n"
"                  settings\n"
"                    ...\n"
"                  requires\n"
"                    dep/0.1#1c90e8b8306c359b103da31faeee824c:9bdee485ef71c14ac5f8a657202632bdb8b4482b"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:177
msgid ""
"We will have these two different binaries, one of them linking with the "
"first revision of the ``dep/0.1`` dependency (with the \"Hello World\" "
"message), and the other binary with the other ``package_id`` linked with the "
"second revision of the ``dep/0.1`` dependency (with the \"Hello Moon\" "
"message)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:179
msgid ""
"The above described mode is called ``full_mode``, and it is the default for "
"the ``embed_mode``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:183
msgid "Package types and default modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:185
msgid ""
"The \"embed/non-embed/unknown\" modes are derived from the recipes "
"definitions of ``package_type``. Recall that ``package_type`` can be "
"explicitly defined as a recipe attribute, but it can also be implicity "
"derived from the ``shared`` option. The resulting ``package_id_mode`` "
"defines when a binary package needs to be built from source, depending on "
"the chanages of the dependency version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:192
msgid ""
"It is very important to have a correct definition of ``package_type``, and "
"it is extremely recommended to define it, either explicitly with "
"``package_type`` recipe attribute, or by the definition of the ``shared`` "
"options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:194
msgid "The following summarizes the defaults:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:198
#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:207
#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:216
#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:224
#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:232
msgid "Package types:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:200
msgid "A ``shared-library`` or ``application`` consuming a ``static-library``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:201
msgid ""
"An ``application``, ``shared-library`` or ``static-library`` consuming a "
"``header-library``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:203
msgid ""
"Default ``package_id_mode``: ``full_mode`` any change (version, recipe, or "
"binary) forces a consumer rebuild"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:209
msgid "A ``static-library`` linking with another ``static-library``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:210
msgid ""
"An ``application`` or ``shared-librayr`` linking another ``shared-library``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:212
msgid ""
"Default ``package_id_mode``: ``minor_mode``: patch-version changes are "
"ignored; minor or major changes force a rebuild"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:214
msgid "Header-only library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:218
msgid ""
"A ``header-library`` depending on any other ``static-library``, ``shared-"
"library`` or ``headed-library``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:220
msgid ""
"Default ``package_id_mode``: None. Header-only libraries are not affected in "
"their ``package_id`` by their dependencies versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:222
msgid "Build mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:226
msgid ""
"Any package doing a ``tool_requires`` to other package (in recipe or by "
"profile injection via ``[tool_requires]``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:228
msgid ""
"Default ``package_id_mode``: None. By default, tools do not change the "
"binary they help to produce (the binary is the same built with different "
"versions of CMake, for example. For compilers this might not be true, but "
"that effect is already captured by ``compiler.version`` setting)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:230
msgid "Unknown mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:234
msgid "When any of the package types are not defined"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:236
msgid ""
"Default ``package_id_mode``: ``semver_mode``: for versions ``>=1.0`` only "
"major changes force a rebuild; for ``<1.0`` any change forces a rebuild"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/binary_model/dependencies.rst:241
msgid ""
"There are different ways to change the defaults, like defining ``core."
"package_id:default_embed_mode``, ``core.package_id:default_non_embed_mode``, "
"and ``core.package_id:default_unknown_mode`` in ``global.conf``, or defining "
"the equivalent recipe attributes. All of this will be explained in following "
"sections."
msgstr ""
